> *"Such a general development cannot be attributed to the false tactics of any single party or to the mistakes of individual leaders. On the contrary, the conduct of individual leaders is determined by the conditions in which they operate."*

 - Karl Kautsky, *Hitlerism and Social Democracy*, 1934

This is a game of alternate history. While historical accuracy is a major concern, keep in mind that this is a *game*, and that any divergence from actual events will necessarily have to involve simplifications and speculation.

For more information on the politics and government of the German Republic, see the "Library" page on the top left. If this is your first time playing the game, it is strongly recommended that you read the overview.

- @1919_easy: Begin (easy difficulty)
- @1919_main: Begin (normal difficulty)
- @1919_hard: Begin (hard difficulty)
- @1919_historical: Begin (historical mode)

@1919_hard
